/-!
# The fundamental group of a manifold with a Heegaard splitting

Let `M` be a `3`-manifold without boundary with a Heegaard splitting of genus `g` into two
handlebodies `H₁` and `H₂` meeting in their common boundary surface, the Heegaard surface
`H₁ ∩ H₂`. Then the inclusion of either handlebody induces a surjection `π₁(Hᵢ) → π₁(M)` at every
base point of `Hᵢ`. Since `π₁(Hᵢ)` is free of rank `g`
(`TauCeti.nonempty_fundamentalGroup_handlebody_mulEquiv_freeGroup`), the fundamental group of `M`
is finitely generated, and its rank, the least number of generators (`Group.rank`), is at most
`g`. Taking a splitting of least genus, the rank of `π₁(M)` is at most the Heegaard genus of `M`.
This is the inequality whose equality case is Waldhausen's rank-versus-genus conjecture
(`TauCeti.RankGenusConjecture`).

More precisely, `π₁(M, x)` at a point `x` of the Heegaard surface is the free product of `π₁(H₁, x)`
and `π₁(H₂, x)` amalgamated over `π₁(H₁ ∩ H₂, x)`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardSplitting.isPushout_fundamentalGroup`). Since the Heegaard surface carries the
fundamental group of each handlebody, `π₁(M, x)` is the quotient of `π₁(H₁ ∩ H₂, x)` by the
subgroup generated by the loops that become trivial in `H₁` and those that become trivial in `H₂`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardSplitting.fundamentalGroup_map_inter_surjective`,
`TauCeti.HeegaardSplitting.ker_fundamentalGroup_map_inter`). This is the group-theoretic form of
the presentation of `π₁(M)` by a Heegaard diagram, in which the two kernels are normally generated
by the `α` and the `β` curves (an identification not made here), and the form from which the first
homology of `M` is computed by abelianization.

Both results are applications of the Seifert–van Kampen theorem
(`TauCeti.FundamentalGroup.range_map_subtypeVal_sup_eq_top`, `TauCeti.isPushout_fundamentalGroup`).
The generation half is applied to the cover of `M` by `H₂` and a thickening `N` of `H₁`: the union
of `H₁` with an open neighbourhood `W₂` of the boundary surface in `H₂` that deformation retracts
onto it (`TauCeti.exists_deformation_frontier_handlebody`). The interiors of `N` and `H₂` cover
`M`, because by invariance of domain the frontier of `H₂` is the boundary surface
(`TauCeti.HeegaardSplitting.coe_mem_left_iff`). Since `N` deformation retracts onto `H₁`, loops in
`N` come from `H₁`; since the boundary surface carries the fundamental group of `H₂`
(`TauCeti.fundamentalGroup_map_frontier_handlebody_surjective`), loops in `H₂` are homotopic in
`H₂` to loops on the boundary surface, which lies in `H₁`. For the amalgamated product, `H₂` is
thickened in the same way by a neighbourhood `W₁` of the boundary surface in `H₁`; the two
thickenings deformation retract onto `H₁` and `H₂`, and their intersection `W₁ ∪ W₂` onto the
Heegaard surface. A pushout of groups along surjections is a quotient of the corner
(`CategoryTheory.IsPushout.ker_comp_eq_sup_of_surjective`), which gives the presentation.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.HeegaardSplitting.fundamentalGroup_map_left_surjective` and
  `TauCeti.HeegaardSplitting.fundamentalGroup_map_right_surjective`: the fundamental group of
  either handlebody surjects onto the fundamental group of the manifold.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardSplitting.fg_fundamentalGroup`: the fundamental group of the manifold is
  finitely generated.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardSplitting.rank_fundamentalGroup_le_genus`: its rank is at most the genus of the
  splitting.
* `TauCeti.rank_fundamentalGroup_le_heegaardGenus`: its rank is at most the Heegaard genus.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardSplitting.isPushout_fundamentalGroup`: the fundamental group of the manifold is
  the free product of those of the handlebodies amalgamated over that of the Heegaard surface.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardSplitting.fundamentalGroup_map_inter_surjective` and
  `TauCeti.HeegaardSplitting.ker_fundamentalGroup_map_inter`: the fundamental group of the
  manifold is the quotient of that of the Heegaard surface by the subgroup generated by the
  kernels of the maps to the two handlebodies.

## References

* J. Hempel, *3-Manifolds*, Annals of Mathematics Studies 86, Princeton University Press (1976),
  Chapter 2.
* M. Scharlemann, *Heegaard splittings of compact 3-manifolds*, in *Handbook of Geometric
  Topology*, North-Holland (2002), Section 2.
* A. Hatcher, *Algebraic Topology*, Cambridge University Press (2002), Section 1.2 (the
  Seifert–van Kampen theorem).
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory Module Set
open scoped ContinuousMap

namespace TauCeti

namespace HeegaardSplitting

variable {E M : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace M]
  [ChartedSpace E M] (s : HeegaardSplitting M)

/-- A handlebody of a splitting has a finitely generated fundamental group, of rank at most the
genus. -/
private theorem exists_fg_rank_le {A : Set M} (e : A ≃ₜ handlebody s.genus) (x : A) :
    ∃ _ : Group.FG (FundamentalGroup A x), Group.rank (FundamentalGroup A x) ≤ s.genus := by
  let φ := e.toHomotopyEquiv.fundamentalGroupMulEquiv x
  have : Group.FG (FundamentalGroup A x) :=
    Group.fg_of_surjective (f := φ.symm.toMonoidHom) φ.symm.surjective
  exact ⟨this, (Group.rank_congr φ).trans_le (rank_fundamentalGroup_handlebody _).le⟩

/-- **The cover of the van Kampen argument.** If `W` is relatively open in the second handlebody
and contains the Heegaard surface, then the interiors of the union of the first handlebody with
`W` and of the second handlebody cover the space. -/
private theorem interior_union_interior_right_eq_univ {W : Set M}
    (hW : IsOpen ((↑) ⁻¹' W : Set s.right)) (hLRW : s.left ∩ s.right ⊆ W) :
    interior (s.left ∪ W) ∪ interior s.right = univ := by
  have hLR (p : M) : p ∈ s.left ∪ s.right := s.union_eq_univ ▸ mem_univ p
  obtain ⟨O, hO, hOW⟩ := isOpen_induced_iff.1 hW
  have hint : O ∪ s.rightᶜ ⊆ interior (s.left ∪ W) := by
    refine interior_maximal ?_ (hO.union s.isClosed_right.isOpen_compl)
    rintro p (hpO | hpR)
    · by_cases hpR : p ∈ s.right
      · have hp : (⟨p, hpR⟩ : s.right) ∈ (↑) ⁻¹' O := hpO
        rw [hOW] at hp
        exact .inr hp
      · exact .inl ((hLR p).resolve_right hpR)
    · exact .inl ((hLR p).resolve_right hpR)
  refine eq_univ_of_forall fun p ↦ ?_
  by_cases hpR : p ∈ s.right
  · by_cases hpL : p ∈ s.left
    · have hp : (⟨p, hpR⟩ : s.right) ∈ (↑) ⁻¹' W := hLRW ⟨hpL, hpR⟩
      rw [← hOW] at hp
      exact .inl (hint (.inl hp))
    · -- A point of the second handlebody off the first is off the frontier of the second.
      refine .inr ?_
      rw [← self_sdiff_frontier, ← s.inter_eq_frontier_right]
      exact ⟨hpR, fun h ↦ hpL h.1⟩
  · exact .inl (hint (.inr hpR))

/-- The Heegaard surface carries the fundamental group of the first handlebody. -/
private theorem fundamentalGroup_map_inclusion_inter_left_surjective (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3)
    (x : ↥(s.left ∩ s.right)) :
    Function.Surjective (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.inclusion inter_subset_left) x) := by
  obtain ⟨eL⟩ := s.nonempty_homeomorph_left
  exact fundamentalGroup_map_inclusion_frontier_surjective inter_subset_left eL
    (fun p ↦ (and_iff_right p.property).trans (s.coe_mem_right_iff hE eL p)) x

/-- The Heegaard surface carries the fundamental group of the second handlebody. -/
private theorem fundamentalGroup_map_inclusion_inter_right_surjective (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3)
    (x : ↥(s.left ∩ s.right)) :
    Function.Surjective (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.inclusion inter_subset_right) x) := by
  obtain ⟨eR⟩ := s.nonempty_homeomorph_right
  exact fundamentalGroup_map_inclusion_frontier_surjective inter_subset_right eR
    (fun p ↦ (and_iff_left p.property).trans (s.coe_mem_left_iff hE eR p)) x

/-- **Loops in the second handlebody come from the first.** At a point of the Heegaard surface,
every loop in the second handlebody is homotopic in it to a loop on the boundary surface, which
lies in the first handlebody. -/
private theorem range_map_right_le_range_map_left (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3)
    (e : s.right ≃ₜ handlebody s.genus)
    (y : {y : handlebody s.genus | (y : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody s.genus)})
    (hy : ((e.symm y : s.right) : M) ∈ s.left) :
    (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal s.right) (e.symm y)).range ≤
      (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal s.left) ⟨_, hy⟩).range := by
  rintro _ ⟨γ, rfl⟩
  -- The loop `γ` is homotopic in the second handlebody to a loop `δ` on the Heegaard surface.
  obtain ⟨δ, rfl⟩ := s.fundamentalGroup_map_inclusion_inter_right_surjective hE
    (⟨_, hy, (e.symm y).property⟩ : ↥(s.left ∩ s.right)) γ
  refine ⟨FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.inclusion inter_subset_left) _ δ, ?_⟩
  -- Both sides are the image of `δ` under the inclusion of the Heegaard surface, read through
  -- either handlebody; the composites of inclusions agree by definition, and as the base point
  -- of the target group depends on the map, the chain closes by unfolding.
  have h₁ := DFunLike.congr_fun (_root_.FundamentalGroup.map_comp
    (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal s.left) (ContinuousMap.inclusion inter_subset_left) _) δ
  have h₂ := DFunLike.congr_fun (_root_.FundamentalGroup.map_comp
    (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal s.right) (ContinuousMap.inclusion inter_subset_right) _) δ
  rw [MonoidHom.comp_apply] at h₁ h₂
  exact h₁.symm.trans h₂

/-! ### Deforming collars of the Heegaard surface -/

section Collar

variable {P Q T : Set M} {g : ℕ} (e : P ≃ₜ handlebody g) {V : Set (handlebody g)}
  (F : C(unitInterval × V, V)) (hTV : ∀ a : T, ∀ ha : (a : M) ∈ P, e ⟨a, ha⟩ ∈ V)

/-- The deformation `F` of a neighbourhood `V` of the boundary surface in the standard
handlebody, read through a handlebody `e : P ≃ₜ handlebody g` of `M` at the points of a set `T`
that lie in `P`, all of which correspond to points of `V`. -/
private noncomputable def collarDeform (q : unitInterval × T) (hq : (q.2 : M) ∈ P) : M :=
  ((e.symm (F (q.1, ⟨e ⟨q.2, hq⟩, hTV q.2 hq⟩)) : P) : M)

private theorem continuous_collarDeform :
    Continuous fun q : {q : unitInterval × T | (q.2 : M) ∈ P} ↦
      collarDeform e F hTV q.val q.property := by
  unfold collarDeform
  fun_prop

private theorem collarDeform_zero (hF₀ : ∀ x, F (0, x) = x) (a : T) (ha : (a : M) ∈ P) :
    collarDeform e F hTV (0, a) ha = a := by
  simp [collarDeform, hF₀]

private theorem collarDeform_of_mem
    (hmem : ∀ p : P, (p : M) ∈ Q ↔ (e p : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody g))
    (hFfix : ∀ t (x : V), ((x : handlebody g) : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody g) →
      F (t, x) = x)
    (q : unitInterval × T) (hqP : (q.2 : M) ∈ P) (hqQ : (q.2 : M) ∈ Q) :
    collarDeform e F hTV q hqP = q.2 := by
  simp [collarDeform, hFfix _ ⟨e ⟨q.2, hqP⟩, hTV q.2 hqP⟩ ((hmem ⟨q.2, hqP⟩).1 hqQ)]

private theorem collarDeform_one_mem
    (hmem : ∀ p : P, (p : M) ∈ Q ↔ (e p : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody g))
    (hF₁ : ∀ x, ((F (1, x) : handlebody g) : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody g))
    (a : T) (ha : (a : M) ∈ P) : collarDeform e F hTV (1, a) ha ∈ Q := by
  rw [collarDeform, hmem, Homeomorph.apply_symm_apply]
  exact hF₁ _

private theorem collarDeform_mem_image (q : unitInterval × T) (hq : (q.2 : M) ∈ P) :
    collarDeform e F hTV q hq ∈ ((↑) '' (e ⁻¹' V) : Set M) :=
  ⟨_, by simp, rfl⟩

/-- The subset of `M` corresponding to a path-connected subset `V` of the standard handlebody
through a handlebody `e : P ≃ₜ handlebody g` of `M` is path connected. -/
private theorem isPathConnected_image_preimage (hVc : IsPathConnected V) :
    IsPathConnected ((↑) '' (e ⁻¹' V) : Set M) := by
  rw [← e.image_symm]
  exact (hVc.image e.symm.continuous).image continuous_subtypeVal

/-- A map on `unitInterval × T` is continuous if it is continuous on the points over each of two
closed sets `L` and `R` covering `M`. -/
private theorem continuous_of_continuous_domRestrict {X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X]
    {L R : Set M} (hL : IsClosed L) (hR : IsClosed R) (hLRu : L ∪ R = univ)
    {H : unitInterval × T → X}
    (hHL : Continuous ({q | (q.2 : M) ∈ L}.domRestrict H))
    (hHR : Continuous ({q | (q.2 : M) ∈ R}.domRestrict H)) : Continuous H := by
  rw [← continuousOn_univ, ← (eq_univ_of_forall fun q ↦ (hLRu ▸ mem_univ _ : (q.2 : M) ∈ L ∪ R) :
    {q : unitInterval × T | (q.2 : M) ∈ L} ∪ {q | (q.2 : M) ∈ R} = univ)]
  exact .union_of_isClosed (continuousOn_iff_continuous_domRestrict.2 hHL)
    (continuousOn_iff_continuous_domRestrict.2 hHR) (hL.preimage (by fun_prop))
    (hR.preimage (by fun_prop))

/-- A point of a handlebody `e : P ≃ₜ handlebody g` of `M` that lies in `Q ∪ W`, where `Q ∩ P`
corresponds to the boundary surface and `W` to a neighbourhood `V` of it, corresponds to a point
of `V`. -/
private theorem apply_mem_of_mem_union_image {P Q : Set M} {g : ℕ} (e : P ≃ₜ handlebody g)
    (hmem : ∀ p : P, (p : M) ∈ Q ↔ (e p : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody g))
    {V : Set (handlebody g)}
    (hSV : {x : handlebody g | (x : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody g)} ⊆ V) {a : M}
    (ha : a ∈ Q ∪ (↑) '' (e ⁻¹' V)) (haP : a ∈ P) : e ⟨a, haP⟩ ∈ V := by
  rcases ha with haQ | ⟨b, hb, hba⟩
  · exact hSV ((hmem ⟨a, haP⟩).1 haQ)
  · rwa [(Subtype.ext hba.symm : (⟨a, haP⟩ : P) = b)]

/-- The points of a handlebody `e : P ≃ₜ handlebody g` of `M` lying in `Q`, which correspond to
the boundary surface, lie in the subset corresponding to a neighbourhood `V` of it. -/
private theorem inter_subset_image {P Q : Set M} {g : ℕ} (e : P ≃ₜ handlebody g)
    (hmem : ∀ p : P, (p : M) ∈ Q ↔ (e p : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody g))
    {V : Set (handlebody g)}
    (hSV : {x : handlebody g | (x : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody g)} ⊆ V) :
    P ∩ Q ⊆ (↑) '' (e ⁻¹' V) :=
  fun p hp ↦ ⟨⟨p, hp.1⟩, hSV ((hmem ⟨p, hp.1⟩).1 hp.2), rfl⟩

end Collar

/-- **A thickened handlebody deformation retracts onto it.** Let `M` be covered by closed sets
`L` and `R` meeting along the frontier of a handlebody `R ≃ₜ handlebody g`, and let `F` deform an
open neighbourhood `V` of the boundary surface in the standard handlebody onto the boundary
surface, fixing it. Let `W` be the corresponding neighbourhood of `L ∩ R` in `R`. Then `L ∪ W`
deformation retracts onto `L`: the deformation is the identity on `L` and `F` on `W`. -/
private theorem exists_homotopyEquiv_union {L R : Set M} (hL : IsClosed L) (hR : IsClosed R)
    (hLRu : L ∪ R = univ) {g : ℕ} (e : R ≃ₜ handlebody g)
    (hmem : ∀ p : R, (p : M) ∈ L ↔ (e p : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody g))
    {V : Set (handlebody g)}
    (hSV : {x : handlebody g | (x : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody g)} ⊆ V)
    (F : C(unitInterval × V, V)) (hF₀ : ∀ x, F (0, x) = x)
    (hF₁ : ∀ x, ((F (1, x) : handlebody g) : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody g))
    (hFfix : ∀ t (x : V), ((x : handlebody g) : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody g) →
      F (t, x) = x) :
    ∃ eN : L ≃ₕ ↥(L ∪ (↑) '' (e ⁻¹' V)), eN.toFun = ContinuousMap.inclusion subset_union_left := by
  classical
  have hLR (p : M) : p ∈ L ∪ R := hLRu ▸ mem_univ p
  have hV (a : ↥(L ∪ (↑) '' (e ⁻¹' V))) (ha : (a : M) ∈ R) : e ⟨a, ha⟩ ∈ V :=
    apply_mem_of_mem_union_image e hmem hSV a.property ha
  -- The deformation is `F` on the points of `R` and the identity on those of `L`.
  let H (q : unitInterval × ↥(L ∪ (↑) '' (e ⁻¹' V))) : M :=
    if hq : (q.2 : M) ∈ R then collarDeform e F hV q hq else q.2
  have hHL (q : unitInterval × ↥(L ∪ (↑) '' (e ⁻¹' V))) (hq : (q.2 : M) ∈ L) : H q = q.2 := by
    simp only [H]
    split_ifs with hqR
    exacts [collarDeform_of_mem e F hV hmem hFfix q hqR hq, rfl]
  have hHR (q : unitInterval × ↥(L ∪ (↑) '' (e ⁻¹' V))) (hq : (q.2 : M) ∈ R) :
      H q = collarDeform e F hV q hq :=
    dite_eq_left_of_eq_true (eq_true hq)
  have hHc : Continuous H := continuous_of_continuous_domRestrict hL hR hLRu
    ((continuous_subtypeVal.comp continuous_snd).comp continuous_subtypeVal |>.congr
      fun q ↦ (hHL q.val q.property).symm)
    ((continuous_collarDeform e F hV).congr fun q ↦ (hHR q.val q.property).symm)
  refine ⟨ContinuousMap.HomotopyEquiv.ofWeakDeformationRetraction subset_union_left H hHc
    (fun q ↦ ?_) (fun a ↦ ?_) (fun a ↦ ?_) (fun t a ha ↦ (hHL (t, a) ha).symm ▸ ha),
    ContinuousMap.ext fun a ↦ Subtype.ext
      (ContinuousMap.HomotopyEquiv.coe_ofWeakDeformationRetraction_apply _ _ _ _ _ _ _ a)⟩
  · by_cases hq : (q.2 : M) ∈ R
    · exact hHR q hq ▸ .inr (collarDeform_mem_image e F hV q hq)
    · exact hHL q ((hLR _).resolve_right hq) ▸ q.2.property
  · by_cases ha : (a : M) ∈ R
    · rw [hHR (0, a) ha, collarDeform_zero e F hV hF₀]
    · exact hHL (0, a) ((hLR a).resolve_right ha)
  · by_cases ha : (a : M) ∈ R
    · exact hHR (1, a) ha ▸ collarDeform_one_mem e F hV hmem hF₁ a ha
    · exact hHL (1, a) ((hLR a).resolve_right ha) ▸ (hLR a).resolve_right ha

/-- **The van Kampen argument.** At some point of the Heegaard surface, the fundamental group of
the first handlebody surjects onto that of the manifold. The space is covered by the second
handlebody and the union `N` of the first with a neighbourhood `W` of the Heegaard surface in the
second; loops in `N` come from the first handlebody since `N` deformation retracts onto it, and
so do loops in the second handlebody. -/
private theorem exists_fundamentalGroup_map_left_surjective (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3) :
    ∃ x : s.left, Function.Surjective
      (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal s.left) x) := by
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := s.nonempty_homeomorph_right
  obtain ⟨V, hVo, hVc, hSV, F, hF₀, hF₁, hFfix⟩ := exists_deformation_frontier_handlebody s.genus
  obtain ⟨eN, heN⟩ := exists_homotopyEquiv_union s.isClosed_left s.isClosed_right
    s.union_eq_univ e (s.coe_mem_left_iff hE e) hSV F hF₀ hF₁ hFfix
  have hWc := isPathConnected_image_preimage e hVc
  let W : Set M := (↑) '' (e ⁻¹' V)
  have hmemW (p : s.right) : (p : M) ∈ W ↔ e p ∈ V := Subtype.val_injective.mem_set_image
  have hLRW {p : M} (hpL : p ∈ s.left) (hpR : p ∈ s.right) : p ∈ W :=
    (hmemW ⟨p, hpR⟩).2 (hSV ((s.coe_mem_left_iff hE e ⟨p, hpR⟩).1 hpL))
  have hNR : (s.left ∪ W) ∩ s.right = W := by
    refine Subset.antisymm ?_ fun p hp ↦ ⟨.inr hp, Subtype.coe_image_subset _ _ hp⟩
    rintro p ⟨hpL | hpW, hpR⟩
    exacts [hLRW hpL hpR, hpW]
  have hcover : interior (s.left ∪ W) ∪ interior s.right = univ :=
    s.interior_union_interior_right_eq_univ
      (by rw [Subtype.val_injective.preimage_image]; exact hVo.preimage e.continuous)
      fun p hp ↦ hLRW hp.1 hp.2
  -- The base point: the point of the Heegaard surface over a point of the boundary surface.
  obtain ⟨y₀, hy₀, -⟩ := isPathConnected_frontier_handlebody s.genus
  let y : {y : handlebody s.genus | (y : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody s.genus)} :=
    ⟨⟨y₀, (isClosed_handlebody s.genus).frontier_subset hy₀⟩, hy₀⟩
  have hyL : ((e.symm y : s.right) : M) ∈ s.left := by
    rw [s.coe_mem_left_iff hE e, Homeomorph.apply_symm_apply]
    exact y.property
  refine ⟨⟨_, hyL⟩, MonoidHom.range_eq_top.1 (eq_top_iff.2 ?_)⟩
  have : PathConnectedSpace s.left :=
    s.nonempty_homeomorph_left.some.symm.toHomotopyEquiv.pathConnectedSpace
  have : PathConnectedSpace s.right := e.symm.toHomotopyEquiv.pathConnectedSpace
  refine (FundamentalGroup.range_map_subtypeVal_sup_eq_top hcover
    (isPathConnected_iff_pathConnectedSpace.2 eN.pathConnectedSpace)
    (isPathConnected_iff_pathConnectedSpace.2 inferInstance) (by rw [hNR]; exact hWc) (.inl hyL)
    (e.symm y).property).ge.trans (sup_le ?_ (s.range_map_right_le_range_map_left hE e y hyL))
  -- Loops in `N` come from the first handlebody.
  have hbij := eN.fundamentalGroup_map_bijective ⟨_, hyL⟩
  rw [heN] at hbij
  rintro _ ⟨γ, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨δ, rfl⟩ := hbij.2 γ
  have h := DFunLike.congr_fun (_root_.FundamentalGroup.map_comp
    (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal (s.left ∪ W)) (ContinuousMap.inclusion subset_union_left)
    ⟨_, hyL⟩) δ
  rw [MonoidHom.comp_apply] at h
  -- The composite `(subtypeVal (s.left ∪ W)).comp (inclusion subset_union_left)` in `h` is
  -- `subtypeVal s.left` by definition; as the base point of the target group depends on the map,
  -- `h` is used up to this unfolding rather than rewritten.
  exact ⟨δ, h⟩

/-- **The fundamental group of the first handlebody of a Heegaard splitting surjects onto that of
the manifold.** For a Heegaard splitting of a manifold without boundary charted on a
three-dimensional real normed space, the inclusion of the first handlebody induces a surjection
of fundamental groups at every base point in it. -/
theorem fundamentalGroup_map_left_surjective (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3) (x : s.left) :
    Function.Surjective (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal s.left) x) := by
  obtain ⟨x₀, hx₀⟩ := s.exists_fundamentalGroup_map_left_surjective hE
  have : PathConnectedSpace s.left :=
    s.nonempty_homeomorph_left.some.symm.toHomotopyEquiv.pathConnectedSpace
  exact FundamentalGroup.map_surjective_of_path _ (PathConnectedSpace.somePath x₀ x) hx₀

/-- **The fundamental group of the second handlebody of a Heegaard splitting surjects onto that of
the manifold.** For a Heegaard splitting of a manifold without boundary charted on a
three-dimensional real normed space, the inclusion of the second handlebody induces a surjection
of fundamental groups at every base point in it. -/
theorem fundamentalGroup_map_right_surjective (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3) (x : s.right) :
    Function.Surjective (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal s.right) x) := by
  have h := s.symm.fundamentalGroup_map_left_surjective hE
  rw [symm_left] at h
  exact h x

include s in
/-- **The fundamental group of a manifold with a Heegaard splitting is finitely generated.** This
holds for a manifold without boundary charted on a three-dimensional real normed space, at every
base point. -/
theorem fg_fundamentalGroup (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3) (x : M) : Group.FG (FundamentalGroup M x) := by
  rcases (s.union_eq_univ ▸ mem_univ x : x ∈ s.left ∪ s.right) with hx | hx
  · obtain ⟨_, -⟩ := s.exists_fg_rank_le s.nonempty_homeomorph_left.some ⟨x, hx⟩
    exact Group.fg_of_surjective (s.fundamentalGroup_map_left_surjective hE ⟨x, hx⟩)
  · obtain ⟨_, -⟩ := s.exists_fg_rank_le s.nonempty_homeomorph_right.some ⟨x, hx⟩
    exact Group.fg_of_surjective (s.fundamentalGroup_map_right_surjective hE ⟨x, hx⟩)

/-- **The rank of the fundamental group is at most the genus of a Heegaard splitting.** For a
manifold without boundary charted on a three-dimensional real normed space, the fundamental group
is generated by as many elements as the genus of any Heegaard splitting, at every base point. -/
theorem rank_fundamentalGroup_le_genus (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3) (x : M)
    [Group.FG (FundamentalGroup M x)] : Group.rank (FundamentalGroup M x) ≤ s.genus := by
  rcases (s.union_eq_univ ▸ mem_univ x : x ∈ s.left ∪ s.right) with hx | hx
  · obtain ⟨_, hrank⟩ :=
      s.exists_fg_rank_le s.nonempty_homeomorph_left.some ⟨x, hx⟩
    exact (Group.rank_le_of_surjective (H := FundamentalGroup M x) _
      (s.fundamentalGroup_map_left_surjective hE ⟨x, hx⟩)).trans hrank
  · obtain ⟨_, hrank⟩ :=
      s.exists_fg_rank_le s.nonempty_homeomorph_right.some ⟨x, hx⟩
    exact (Group.rank_le_of_surjective (H := FundamentalGroup M x) _
      (s.fundamentalGroup_map_right_surjective hE ⟨x, hx⟩)).trans hrank

/-! ### The fundamental group as an amalgamated product -/

/-- **The thickened Heegaard surface deformation retracts onto it.** Let `F` deform an open
neighbourhood `V` of the boundary surface in the standard handlebody onto the boundary surface,
fixing it, and let `W₁` and `W₂` be the corresponding neighbourhoods of the Heegaard surface in
the first and the second handlebody. Then the intersection of `H₁ ∪ W₂` with `H₂ ∪ W₁`, which is
`W₁ ∪ W₂`, deformation retracts onto the Heegaard surface: the deformation is `F` on `W₁` and on
`W₂`. -/
private theorem exists_homotopyEquiv_inter (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3)
    (eL : s.left ≃ₜ handlebody s.genus) (eR : s.right ≃ₜ handlebody s.genus)
    {V : Set (handlebody s.genus)}
    (hSV : {x : handlebody s.genus | (x : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody s.genus)} ⊆ V)
    (F : C(unitInterval × V, V)) (hF₀ : ∀ x, F (0, x) = x)
    (hF₁ : ∀ x, ((F (1, x) : handlebody s.genus) : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody s.genus))
    (hFfix : ∀ t (x : V), ((x : handlebody s.genus) : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody s.genus) →
      F (t, x) = x) :
    ∃ eN : ↥(s.left ∩ s.right) ≃ₕ
        ↥((s.left ∪ (↑) '' (eR ⁻¹' V)) ∩ (s.right ∪ (↑) '' (eL ⁻¹' V))),
      eN.toFun = ContinuousMap.inclusion (inter_subset_inter subset_union_left subset_union_left)
      := by
  classical
  have hmemL (p : s.left) := s.coe_mem_right_iff hE eL p
  have hmemR (p : s.right) := s.coe_mem_left_iff hE eR p
  have hLR (p : M) : p ∈ s.left ∪ s.right := s.union_eq_univ ▸ mem_univ p
  have hVR (a : ↥((s.left ∪ (↑) '' (eR ⁻¹' V)) ∩ (s.right ∪ (↑) '' (eL ⁻¹' V))))
      (ha : (a : M) ∈ s.right) : eR ⟨a, ha⟩ ∈ V :=
    apply_mem_of_mem_union_image eR hmemR hSV a.property.1 ha
  have hVL (a : ↥((s.left ∪ (↑) '' (eR ⁻¹' V)) ∩ (s.right ∪ (↑) '' (eL ⁻¹' V))))
      (ha : (a : M) ∈ s.left) : eL ⟨a, ha⟩ ∈ V :=
    apply_mem_of_mem_union_image eL hmemL hSV a.property.2 ha
  -- The deformation is `F` on each handlebody; both fix the Heegaard surface.
  let H (q : unitInterval × ↥((s.left ∪ (↑) '' (eR ⁻¹' V)) ∩ (s.right ∪ (↑) '' (eL ⁻¹' V)))) :
      M :=
    if hq : (q.2 : M) ∈ s.right then collarDeform eR F hVR q hq
    else collarDeform eL F hVL q ((hLR q.2).resolve_right hq)
  have hHL (q : unitInterval × ↥((s.left ∪ (↑) '' (eR ⁻¹' V)) ∩ (s.right ∪ (↑) '' (eL ⁻¹' V))))
      (hq : (q.2 : M) ∈ s.left) : H q = collarDeform eL F hVL q hq := by
    simp only [H]
    split_ifs with hqR
    exacts [(collarDeform_of_mem eR F hVR hmemR hFfix q hqR hq).trans
      (collarDeform_of_mem eL F hVL hmemL hFfix q hq hqR).symm, rfl]
  have hHR (q : unitInterval × ↥((s.left ∪ (↑) '' (eR ⁻¹' V)) ∩ (s.right ∪ (↑) '' (eL ⁻¹' V))))
      (hq : (q.2 : M) ∈ s.right) : H q = collarDeform eR F hVR q hq :=
    dite_eq_left_of_eq_true (eq_true hq)
  have hHc : Continuous H := continuous_of_continuous_domRestrict s.isClosed_left s.isClosed_right
    s.union_eq_univ
    ((continuous_collarDeform eL F hVL).congr fun q ↦ (hHL q.val q.property).symm)
    ((continuous_collarDeform eR F hVR).congr fun q ↦ (hHR q.val q.property).symm)
  refine ⟨ContinuousMap.HomotopyEquiv.ofWeakDeformationRetraction
    (inter_subset_inter subset_union_left subset_union_left) H hHc
    (fun q ↦ ?_) (fun a ↦ ?_) (fun a ↦ ?_) (fun t a ha ↦ (hHL (t, a) ha.1).symm ▸
      (collarDeform_of_mem eL F hVL hmemL hFfix (t, a) ha.1 ha.2).symm ▸ ha),
    ContinuousMap.ext fun a ↦ Subtype.ext
      (ContinuousMap.HomotopyEquiv.coe_ofWeakDeformationRetraction_apply _ _ _ _ _ _ _ a)⟩
  · -- The deformation of a point of `W₂` stays in `W₂`, and that of a point of `W₁` in `W₁`.
    by_cases hq : (q.2 : M) ∈ s.right
    · exact hHR q hq ▸ ⟨.inr (collarDeform_mem_image eR F hVR q hq), .inl (Subtype.coe_prop _)⟩
    · have hqL := (hLR q.2).resolve_right hq
      exact hHL q hqL ▸ ⟨.inl (Subtype.coe_prop _), .inr (collarDeform_mem_image eL F hVL q hqL)⟩
  · by_cases ha : (a : M) ∈ s.right
    · rw [hHR (0, a) ha, collarDeform_zero eR F hVR hF₀]
    · rw [hHL (0, a) ((hLR a).resolve_right ha), collarDeform_zero eL F hVL hF₀]
  · by_cases ha : (a : M) ∈ s.right
    · exact hHR (1, a) ha ▸ ⟨collarDeform_one_mem eR F hVR hmemR hF₁ a ha, Subtype.coe_prop _⟩
    · have haL := (hLR a).resolve_right ha
      exact hHL (1, a) haL ▸ ⟨Subtype.coe_prop _, collarDeform_one_mem eL F hVL hmemL hF₁ a haL⟩

/-- **The overlap of the thickened handlebodies is path connected.** If `V` is a path-connected
neighbourhood of the boundary surface in the standard handlebody and `W₁`, `W₂` are the
corresponding neighbourhoods of the Heegaard surface in the two handlebodies, then
`(H₁ ∪ W₂) ∩ (H₂ ∪ W₁) = W₁ ∪ W₂` is path connected. -/
private theorem isPathConnected_inter (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3) (eL : s.left ≃ₜ handlebody s.genus)
    (eR : s.right ≃ₜ handlebody s.genus) {V : Set (handlebody s.genus)} (hVc : IsPathConnected V)
    (hSV : {x : handlebody s.genus | (x : ℂ × ℝ) ∈ frontier (handlebody s.genus)} ⊆ V) {x : M}
    (hxL : x ∈ s.left) (hxR : x ∈ s.right) :
    IsPathConnected ((s.left ∪ (↑) '' (eR ⁻¹' V)) ∩ (s.right ∪ (↑) '' (eL ⁻¹' V))) := by
  have hSWL := inter_subset_image eL (s.coe_mem_right_iff hE eL) hSV
  have hSWR := (inter_comm s.left s.right).subset.trans
    (inter_subset_image eR (s.coe_mem_left_iff hE eR) hSV)
  have hAB : (s.left ∪ (↑) '' (eR ⁻¹' V)) ∩ (s.right ∪ (↑) '' (eL ⁻¹' V)) =
      (↑) '' (eL ⁻¹' V) ∪ (↑) '' (eR ⁻¹' V) := by
    refine Subset.antisymm ?_ (union_subset (subset_inter
      ((Subtype.coe_image_subset _ _).trans subset_union_left) subset_union_right)
      (subset_inter subset_union_right ((Subtype.coe_image_subset _ _).trans subset_union_left)))
    rintro p ⟨hpL | hpWR, hpR | hpWL⟩
    exacts [.inr (hSWR ⟨hpL, hpR⟩), .inl hpWL, .inr hpWR, .inr hpWR]
  exact hAB ▸ (isPathConnected_image_preimage eL hVc).union (isPathConnected_image_preimage eR hVc)
    ⟨x, hSWL ⟨hxL, hxR⟩, hSWR ⟨hxL, hxR⟩⟩

/-- **The Seifert–van Kampen theorem for a Heegaard splitting.** For a Heegaard splitting of a
manifold without boundary charted on a three-dimensional real normed space, and a point `x` of
the Heegaard surface `H₁ ∩ H₂`, the square of fundamental groups at `x` induced by the inclusions
of the Heegaard surface into the two handlebodies `H₁` and `H₂` and of the handlebodies into the
manifold is a pushout of groups. That is, `π₁(M, x)` is the free product of `π₁(H₁, x)` and
`π₁(H₂, x)` amalgamated over `π₁(H₁ ∩ H₂, x)`. -/
theorem isPushout_fundamentalGroup (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3) {x : M} (hxL : x ∈ s.left)
    (hxR : x ∈ s.right) :
    IsPushout
      (GrpCat.ofHom (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.inclusion inter_subset_left)
        (⟨x, hxL, hxR⟩ : ↥(s.left ∩ s.right))))
      (GrpCat.ofHom (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.inclusion inter_subset_right)
        (⟨x, hxL, hxR⟩ : ↥(s.left ∩ s.right))))
      (GrpCat.ofHom (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal s.left) ⟨x, hxL⟩))
      (GrpCat.ofHom (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal s.right) ⟨x, hxR⟩)) := by
  obtain ⟨eL⟩ := s.nonempty_homeomorph_left
  obtain ⟨eR⟩ := s.nonempty_homeomorph_right
  obtain ⟨V, hVo, hVc, hSV, F, hF₀, hF₁, hFfix⟩ := exists_deformation_frontier_handlebody s.genus
  -- Van Kampen applies to the thickened handlebodies `A = H₁ ∪ W₂` and `B = H₂ ∪ W₁`, where `Wᵢ`
  -- is a collar of the Heegaard surface in `Hᵢ`. Each deformation retracts onto its handlebody,
  -- and their intersection `W₁ ∪ W₂` onto the Heegaard surface.
  obtain ⟨eA, heA⟩ := exists_homotopyEquiv_union s.isClosed_left s.isClosed_right
    s.union_eq_univ eR (s.coe_mem_left_iff hE eR) hSV F hF₀ hF₁ hFfix
  obtain ⟨eB, heB⟩ := exists_homotopyEquiv_union s.isClosed_right s.isClosed_left
    ((union_comm _ _).trans s.union_eq_univ) eL (s.coe_mem_right_iff hE eL) hSV F hF₀ hF₁ hFfix
  obtain ⟨eAB, heAB⟩ := s.exists_homotopyEquiv_inter hE eL eR hSV F hF₀ hF₁ hFfix
  have hcover : interior (s.left ∪ (↑) '' (eR ⁻¹' V)) ∪
      interior (s.right ∪ (↑) '' (eL ⁻¹' V)) = univ :=
    eq_univ_of_univ_subset <| (s.interior_union_interior_right_eq_univ
      (by rw [Subtype.val_injective.preimage_image]; exact hVo.preimage eR.continuous)
      ((inter_comm s.left s.right).subset.trans
        (inter_subset_image eR (s.coe_mem_left_iff hE eR) hSV))).ge.trans
      (union_subset_union_right _ (interior_mono subset_union_left))
  have : PathConnectedSpace s.left := eL.symm.toHomotopyEquiv.pathConnectedSpace
  have : PathConnectedSpace s.right := eR.symm.toHomotopyEquiv.pathConnectedSpace
  have hvk := TauCeti.isPushout_fundamentalGroup hcover
    (isPathConnected_iff_pathConnectedSpace.2 eA.pathConnectedSpace)
    (isPathConnected_iff_pathConnectedSpace.2 eB.pathConnectedSpace)
    (s.isPathConnected_inter hE eL eR hVc hSV hxL hxR)
    (Or.inl hxL : x ∈ s.left ∪ (↑) '' (eR ⁻¹' V)) (Or.inl hxR : x ∈ s.right ∪ (↑) '' (eL ⁻¹' V))
  -- Transport the square along the isomorphisms induced by the three retractions; all the maps
  -- are induced by inclusions, so the four compatibility squares commute on representatives.
  have hbij {S T : Set M} (hST : S ⊆ T) (e : S ≃ₕ T) (he : e.toFun = ContinuousMap.inclusion hST)
      (y : S) : Function.Bijective (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.inclusion hST) y) := by
    have h := e.fundamentalGroup_map_bijective y
    rwa [he] at h
  refine hvk.of_iso' (MulEquiv.ofBijective _ (hbij _ eAB heAB ⟨x, hxL, hxR⟩)).toGrpIso
    (MulEquiv.ofBijective _ (hbij _ eA heA ⟨x, hxL⟩)).toGrpIso
    (MulEquiv.ofBijective _ (hbij _ eB heB ⟨x, hxR⟩)).toGrpIso (Iso.refl _) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ <;>
  · ext ⟨γ⟩
    induction γ using Path.Homotopic.Quotient.ind
    rfl

/-- The fundamental group of the Heegaard surface maps to that of the manifold through either
handlebody. -/
private theorem fundamentalGroup_map_subtypeVal_comp_inclusion_inter_left {x : M}
    (hxL : x ∈ s.left) (hxR : x ∈ s.right) :
    (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal s.left) ⟨x, hxL⟩).comp
        (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.inclusion inter_subset_left)
          (⟨x, hxL, hxR⟩ : ↥(s.left ∩ s.right))) =
      FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal (s.left ∩ s.right)) ⟨x, hxL, hxR⟩ :=
  -- `subtypeVal s.left ∘ inclusion` is `subtypeVal (s.left ∩ s.right)` by definition.
  (_root_.FundamentalGroup.map_comp _ _ _).symm

/-- **The Heegaard surface carries the fundamental group of the manifold.** For a Heegaard
splitting of a manifold without boundary charted on a three-dimensional real normed space, the
inclusion of the Heegaard surface induces a surjection of fundamental groups at each of its
points. -/
theorem fundamentalGroup_map_inter_surjective (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3) {x : M} (hxL : x ∈ s.left)
    (hxR : x ∈ s.right) :
    Function.Surjective
      (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal (s.left ∩ s.right)) ⟨x, hxL, hxR⟩) := by
  have h := (s.isPushout_fundamentalGroup hE hxL hxR).surjective_comp_of_surjective
    (s.fundamentalGroup_map_inclusion_inter_left_surjective hE _)
    (s.fundamentalGroup_map_inclusion_inter_right_surjective hE _)
  rw [← s.fundamentalGroup_map_subtypeVal_comp_inclusion_inter_left hxL hxR]
  exact h

/-- **The fundamental group of a Heegaard-split manifold is a quotient of that of the Heegaard
surface.** For a Heegaard splitting of a manifold without boundary charted on a
three-dimensional real normed space, and a point `x` of the Heegaard surface, a loop on the
Heegaard surface is trivial in the manifold exactly when it lies in the subgroup generated by the
loops that are trivial in the first handlebody and those that are trivial in the second. With
`TauCeti.HeegaardSplitting.fundamentalGroup_map_inter_surjective`, this identifies `π₁(M, x)`
with the quotient of `π₁(H₁ ∩ H₂, x)` by these two kernels. -/
theorem ker_fundamentalGroup_map_inter (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3) {x : M} (hxL : x ∈ s.left)
    (hxR : x ∈ s.right) :
    (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal (s.left ∩ s.right)) ⟨x, hxL, hxR⟩).ker =
      (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.inclusion inter_subset_left)
          (⟨x, hxL, hxR⟩ : ↥(s.left ∩ s.right))).ker ⊔
        (FundamentalGroup.map (ContinuousMap.inclusion inter_subset_right)
          (⟨x, hxL, hxR⟩ : ↥(s.left ∩ s.right))).ker := by
  have h := (s.isPushout_fundamentalGroup hE hxL hxR).ker_comp_eq_sup_of_surjective
    (s.fundamentalGroup_map_inclusion_inter_left_surjective hE _)
    (s.fundamentalGroup_map_inclusion_inter_right_surjective hE _)
  rw [← s.fundamentalGroup_map_subtypeVal_comp_inclusion_inter_left hxL hxR]
  exact h

end HeegaardSplitting

/-- **The rank of the fundamental group is at most the Heegaard genus.** For a manifold without
boundary charted on a three-dimensional real normed space and admitting a Heegaard splitting, the
fundamental group is generated by as many elements as its Heegaard genus, at every base point.
Waldhausen's rank-versus-genus conjecture (`TauCeti.RankGenusConjecture`) asks for equality. -/
theorem rank_fundamentalGroup_le_heegaardGenus {E M : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [NormedSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace E M] (hE : finrank ℝ E = 3)
    [Nonempty (HeegaardSplitting M)] (x : M) [Group.FG (FundamentalGroup M x)] :
    Group.rank (FundamentalGroup M x) ≤ heegaardGenus M := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := exists_genus_eq_heegaardGenus M
  exact hs ▸ s.rank_fundamentalGroup_le_genus hE x

end TauCeti
